From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:23:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: free queue when userq fence driver alloc fails

CVE-2026-68103 backport (a609b6278bf3) makes
amdgpu_userq_fence_driver_alloc() return -EBUSY when the doorbell
index is already in adev->userq_xa. Userspace can trigger this.

The error path in amdgpu_userq_create() only unlocks. It leaks the
queue, its userq_va_list entries, the doorbell BO pin and reference,
and the runtime PM reference from pm_runtime_get_sync().

Release these on that error path, as upstream does in its clean_mqd
path.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_userq.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_userq.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_userq.c
index a0bf7c82b83b..546c12e8d995 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_userq.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_userq.c
@@ -584,7 +584,21 @@ amdgpu_userq_create(struct drm_file *filp, union drm_amdgpu_userq *args)
 	xa_init_flags(&queue->fence_drv_xa, XA_FLAGS_ALLOC);
 	r = amdgpu_userq_fence_driver_alloc(adev, queue);
 	if (r) {
+		struct amdgpu_userq_va_cursor *va_cursor, *tmp;
+
 		drm_file_err(uq_mgr->file, "Failed to alloc fence driver\n");
+		if (!amdgpu_bo_reserve(queue->db_obj.obj, true)) {
+			amdgpu_bo_unpin(queue->db_obj.obj);
+			amdgpu_bo_unreserve(queue->db_obj.obj);
+		}
+		amdgpu_bo_unref(&queue->db_obj.obj);
+		list_for_each_entry_safe(va_cursor, tmp, &queue->userq_va_list, list) {
+			list_del(&va_cursor->list);
+			kfree(va_cursor);
+		}
+		kfree(queue);
+		pm_runtime_mark_last_busy(adev_to_drm(adev)->dev);
+		pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(adev_to_drm(adev)->dev);
 		goto unlock;
 	}
 
